# INDAI_MASTER_SPEC.md — DEEP AUDIT REPORT

**Auditor role:** Senior Engineering Architect (20yr experience)
**Date:** 2026-02-07
**Subject:** INDAI_MASTER_SPEC.md — completeness, maturity, value, gaps
**Methodology:** Section-by-section analysis → Cross-reference with SKILL.md → Gap matrix → Recommendations

---

## EXECUTIVE SUMMARY

The MASTER_SPEC is a **governance-level intent document** — it successfully communicates *what the project wants to be*. However, it currently operates at **~35% maturity** as a true engineering specification. It lacks enforceability, measurability, and critical technical definitions that a production frontend project requires.

**Verdict:** Strong vision. Weak specification. Needs 3 layers of reinforcement to become an engineering canon.

| Dimension | Score | Comment |
|-----------|-------|---------|
| Clarity of intent | 9/10 | Excellent — unambiguous governance voice |
| Structural completeness | 4/10 | Missing 6+ critical sections |
| Technical precision | 2/10 | Almost no enforceable technical rules |
| Cross-reference integrity | 3/10 | References documents but doesn't validate them |
| Contradiction safety | 5/10 | Has hierarchy, but no conflict resolution protocol |
| Scalability | 4/10 | Works for 1 developer; breaks at 3+ |

