| 1 | No i18n/language policy for content | UI is Russian (per SKILL.md), but spec says "English only" for repo. Where's the boundary? |
| 2 | No content schema | What fields does a service page MD need? (title, slug, description, price, image?) |
| 3 | No image/media management rules | Where do images live? Naming? Formats? Max size? |
| 4 | No SEO metadata requirements | title, description, OG tags — per page or global? |
| 5 | No content review/approval process | Who approves new service pages? |
| 6 | "Pages are generated from MD" — but no generation rules | Which MD fields map to which components? |

**Recommendation — expand §7:**
```markdown
## 7. CONTENT RULES

### 7.1 Language Policy
| Context | Language |
|---------|----------|
| File names, paths, code, variables | English |
| Documentation (governance, specs) | English |
| User-facing UI text, content | Russian |
| URL slugs | English (kebab-case) |
| Git commits, PR descriptions | English |

### 7.2 Service Page Schema (Markdown Frontmatter)
Every service content file MUST include:
---
title: "Очистка теплообменников"
slug: "heat-exchanger-cleaning"
description: "..."
