### §9. CHANGE MANAGEMENT — 🔴 Critically Weak

Three lines for change management on a production project.

**Gaps:**

| # | Missing | Risk |
|---|---------|------|
| 1 | No branching strategy | Direct pushes to main? |
| 2 | No PR review requirements | Who approves? How many reviewers? |
| 3 | No deployment process | How does code reach production? |
| 4 | No rollback procedure | What if a deploy breaks production? |
| 5 | No environment definitions | dev / staging / production? |
| 6 | No version strategy for the site | How are releases tracked? |
| 7 | "No silent refactors" — undefined | What constitutes "silent"? |

**Recommendation — expand §9:**
```markdown
## 9. CHANGE MANAGEMENT

### 9.1 Branching Strategy
- main: production-ready, protected
- develop: integration branch
- feat/*, fix/*, docs/*: working branches
- No direct commits to main or develop

### 9.2 Pull Request Rules
- Every change requires a PR
- PR must reference the spec section it relates to
- Structural changes require MASTER_SPEC update in the same PR
- Minimum 1 reviewer approval before merge

### 9.3 Deployment
- Production deploys from main only
- Staging auto-deploys from develop
- Rollback: revert merge commit on main

### 9.4 Document Changes
- Any change to /docs/00_GOVERNANCE requires owner approval
- All spec changes tracked in CHANGELOG section of this document
- Deprecated documents moved to 99_ARCHIVE with SUPERSEDED header
```

